{
  "content": {
    "items": [
      {
        "description": "planned (not built) · in-progress · implemented (exists in code) · verified (behavior proven) · drift (code moved, spec stale) · broken (proven failing) · missing (spec claims it, code lacks it) · deprecated.",
        "enforcement": "strict",
        "id": "7e62c43d-63f2-41f6-891e-f2eb39e97a94",
        "status": "verified",
        "text": "Vocabulary — use exactly these meanings"
      },
      {
        "description": "After implementing or verifying ANYTHING, set-status --unit each touched unit. Unit statuses are the feature checklist the user reads.",
        "enforcement": "strict",
        "id": "c993374e-8701-42a3-a448-03b2ce4d7196",
        "status": "verified",
        "text": "Set statuses at both levels, never only the pebble"
      },
      {
        "description": "implemented requires the code to exist; verified requires proven behavior (a run, a test). When reality differs from the spec, set drift/missing/broken truthfully.",
        "enforcement": "strict",
        "id": "b8826989-bd12-4878-983c-09e34c987046",
        "status": "verified",
        "text": "Only claim what you verified"
      },
      {
        "description": "query --status <s> at pebble level; query --unit-status <s> matches checklist items / table fields / workflow nodes and returns the matching units.",
        "enforcement": "strict",
        "id": "1120508e-026b-420b-9a16-a6546fba4f18",
        "status": "verified",
        "text": "Find work by status"
      }
    ],
    "kind": "checklist"
  },
  "createdAt": "2026-07-21T14:32:38.681Z",
  "description": "Statuses ARE the product: they tell the user what is implemented and what is not, at BOTH levels — the pebble and each unit (checklist item, table field, workflow node).",
  "id": "02075798-780c-41c7-8a97-c3751eede040",
